.TH HYPRIDLE 1 "July 2025" "hypridle" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hypridle \- Idle daemon for Hyprland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hypridle
[\fB\-c\fR \fIconfig_path\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Hypridle is a lightweight and efficient Wayland idle daemon designed for the
Hyprland compositor.

It implements the ext-idle-notify-v1 protocol and supports:
.IP \[bu] 2
DBus \fIloginctl\fR lock/unlock and before-sleep hooks
.IP \[bu] 2
DBus inhibit interface (used by Firefox, Steam, etc.)

.SH USAGE
Hypridle should ideally be launched automatically after login. This can be done
via your compositor or systemd.

To launch from Hyprland, add the following to your \fIhyprland.conf\fR:
.PP
.RS
exec-once = hypridle
.RE

To run hypridle using systemd:
.PP
.RS
systemctl --user enable --now hypridle.service
.RE

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fIconfig_path\fR
Specify an alternate configuration file. Defaults to:
\fB${XDG_CONFIG_HOME}/hypr/hypridle.conf\fR
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress output.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output for debugging.

